<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Riccheri Law</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Riccheri Law was the Argentine law of 1901 that introduced compulsory military service for young men, named after the minister of war, Pablo Riccheri. Passed during a naval and military rivalry with Chile, it created a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conscription">conscript</a> army and was also meant to integrate the sons of immigrants into the nation.</p></div>
